  "facts": [
    "Svartis Tunnel, Norway's longest road tunnel at its 1986 opening, stretched 7,614 metres beneath the Svartisen glacier, linking Kilvik to Fykanvatnet on County Road 17.",
    "Built with a pioneering 6.25‑metre diameter tunnel boring machine, Svartis Tunnel remains too narrow for a center line, a unique engineering quirk among Norwegian tunnels.",
    "Condensation inside Svartis Tunnel frequently fogs vehicle windshields, a notorious hazard that has prompted strict closures to pedestrians and cyclists for safety."
